  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In an August 15, 2025 X post, Mark Meador said that innovative AI does not mean predatory AI and that Americans deserve the truth about Big Tech experiments on vulnerable children. On September 11, 2025, he said AI chatbots are products whose makers have a responsibility to comply with consumer protection laws, and he supported the Commission’s study of chatbot functions and behaviors. In a September 11, 2025 X post, he described the FTC as launching a major, sector-wide inquiry into AI chatbots used by Americans, including children. In March 2026, he said AI and data-driven markets may present new factual settings but long-standing governing principles can be applied, and that AI and data analytics can improve enforcement agencies’ investigative speed and accuracy.",
   "sids": [
    "s7",
    "s1",
    "s2",
    "s6",
    "s4",
    "s5"
   ],
   "sentences": [
